### 4. Register the service in `Program.cs`
Add `using RecipeShare.Services;` at the top and `builder.Services.AddSingleton<RecipeService>();` after the `AddRazorComponents` line.

### 5. Update NavMenu
Edit `Components/Layout/NavMenu.razor` to have these nav links:
- Home (`/`)
- Browse Recipes (`/recipes`)
- Submit Recipe (`/recipes/submit`)

Remove the Counter and Weather nav items. Keep the existing structure/styling.

### 6. Update `Components/Pages/Home.razor` (static SSR)
Replace the default content. Show a welcome message and recipe category cards that link to `/recipes/{category}`. Inject `RecipeService` to get categories. Use Bootstrap cards in a grid layout. This is static SSR — no `@rendermode` needed.

```razor
@page "/"
@using RecipeShare.Services
@inject RecipeService RecipeService

<PageTitle>RecipeShare — Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Welcome to RecipeShare</h1>
<p class="lead">Discover and share delicious recipes from around the world.</p>

<h2 class="mt-4 mb-3">Browse by Category</h2>

<div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-3 g-4">
    @foreach (var category in RecipeService.GetCategories())
    {
        <div class="col">
            <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">
                    <h5 class="card-title">@category</h5>
