### 9. Create `Components/Pages/RecipeDetail.razor` (static SSR page, embeds interactive StarRating)
The page itself is static SSR. It embeds the `StarRating` component which has its own `@rendermode`.

```razor
@page "/recipes/detail/{Id:int}"
@using RecipeShare.Services
@using RecipeShare.Models
@inject RecipeService RecipeService

<PageTitle>@(recipe?.Title ?? "Recipe") — RecipeShare</PageTitle>

@if (recipe is null)
{
    <div class="alert alert-warning">Recipe not found.</div>
    <a href="/recipes" class="btn btn-secondary">Back to Recipes</a>
}
else
{
    <nav aria-label="breadcrumb">
        <ol class="breadcrumb">
            <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/recipes">All Categories</a></li>
            <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/recipes/@Uri.EscapeDataString(recipe.Category)">@recipe.Category</a></li>
            <li class="breadcrumb-item active">@recipe.Title</li>
        </ol>
    </nav>

    <h1>@recipe.Title</h1>
    <p class="lead text-muted">@recipe.Description</p>

    @if (recipe.RatingCount > 0)
    {
        <p>⭐ @recipe.AverageRating.ToString("F1") average — @recipe.RatingCount rating(s)</p>
    }

    <h3>Rate this Recipe</h3>
    <StarRating RecipeId="recipe.Id" />

    <hr />

    <h3>Ingredients</h3>
    <ul class="list-group list-group-flush mb-4">
        @foreach (var ingredient in recipe.Ingredients)
        {
